      <h2 class="section-title section-title-glow">Preparing the business case</h2>
      <h3>Market data</h3>
      <p>Research what your role and level pays in your market. Sources: Levels.fyi (for tech), Glassdoor, LinkedIn Salary, Radford data (if you have access), and job postings for your title at comparable companies. Use 3+ sources to triangulate. Screenshot or print relevant data — you may share it in the conversation.</p>
      <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Your accomplishment list</h3>
      <p>Document your last 12 months of impact — quantified. Not tasks, not effort, outcomes. For each accomplishment: what you did, what you owned, what the measurable result was.</p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Revenue, cost, or efficiency impact with numbers</li>
        <li>Projects you led or shipped ahead of schedule</li>
        <li>Scope increases — if you are doing more than your title suggests</li>
        <li>Comparables — if peers at your level at other companies earn more</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Your specific number</h3>
      <p>Before the conversation, know your target number. It should be at the intersection of market rate and your demonstrated scope. Do not go into the conversation to "see what they say" — go in with a number and make the case for it.</p>
